1
00:00:09,480 --> 00:00:12,920
Try brightening it up and stepping away.

2
00:00:23,100 --> 00:00:28,420
Like someone is calling
out to you after the rain.

3
00:00:29,840 --> 00:00:35,300
Walking while looking back,
held by Mom's hand.

4
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:42,420
Hey, that strange feeling I had back then.

5
00:00:43,100 --> 00:00:47,700
So, on the arcade guide tiles,

6
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:53,480
I tried walking only on the black parts.

7
00:00:55,840 --> 00:01:01,780
Everyone was a child once,
but they've all forgotten.

8
00:01:02,720 --> 00:01:09,060
Politicians with their self-important faces,
and aunties with blue eyeshadow too.

9
00:01:09,570 --> 00:01:14,660
Go on, turn that corner over there.

10
00:01:15,700 --> 00:01:19,880
You can meet everyone, everyone.

11
00:01:22,080 --> 00:01:27,800
Kame-ari is over there
surely Kame-ari is there.

12
00:01:29,040 --> 00:01:32,980
Everyone, come on over to our town.

13
00:01:33,880 --> 00:01:34,580
Thank you.

14
00:01:41,640 --> 00:01:42,920
I slept wrong.

15
00:01:58,540 --> 00:02:01,200
Damn it, what a day!

16
00:02:02,880 --> 00:02:05,120
The worst day of my life.

17
00:02:08,160 --> 00:02:11,260
Be gentler, will ya!

18
00:02:11,260 --> 00:02:11,880
Sorry.

19
00:02:11,880 --> 00:02:13,020
Reiko!

20
00:02:13,020 --> 00:02:16,920
With a scrape that big,
it'd hurt no matter who treated it.

21
00:02:18,680 --> 00:02:19,520
Fine, I won't.

22
00:02:19,520 --> 00:02:21,220
Are you all right, senpai?

23
00:02:21,220 --> 00:02:22,700
Reiko, you demon!

24
00:02:22,700 --> 00:02:25,500
It's better to get the painful
stuff over with quickly, right?

25
00:02:25,500 --> 00:02:27,740
Today's Butsumetsu. An unlucky day.

26
00:02:29,040 --> 00:02:30,180
So what?

27
00:02:30,180 --> 00:02:33,140
No, I just had a bad feeling.

28
00:02:33,420 --> 00:02:35,325
If Butsumetsu is supposed to be unlucky,

29
00:02:35,375 --> 00:02:38,220
then everyone should be in for a painful time,
shouldn't they?

30
00:02:38,420 --> 00:02:40,760
No, no, no, I don't want that.

31
00:02:41,280 --> 00:02:44,800
No. Ryo-chan's luck today is the worst.

32
00:02:45,180 --> 00:02:45,960
Luck?

33
00:02:46,280 --> 00:02:49,920
This whole weekly magazine is
full of different fortune-telling.

34
00:02:51,040 --> 00:02:54,380
When I check Ryo-chan's fortune,
born March 3rd, using Sensei-jutsu,

35
00:02:55,220 --> 00:02:57,400
today is the worst day in a hundred years.

36
00:02:57,400 --> 00:03:00,820
No money luck, no work luck, no love luck.

37
00:03:00,820 --> 00:03:04,120
It says there's a high chance
you'll be caught in a major accident.

38
00:03:05,700 --> 00:03:07,340
Don't say something that
isn't even a performance.

39
00:03:07,940 --> 00:03:08,300
No way...

40
00:03:14,280 --> 00:03:15,000
That hurts!

41
00:03:16,240 --> 00:03:17,380
It's coming true.

42
00:03:17,380 --> 00:03:20,000
It says to watch out for rolling pencils.

43
00:03:20,420 --> 00:03:22,980
That's an eerily accurate prediction,
isn't it?

44
00:03:22,980 --> 00:03:24,280
It's just a coincidence.

45
00:03:24,280 --> 00:03:26,420
If today's fortune is that bad,

46
00:03:26,820 --> 00:03:29,460
how about ending today early?

47
00:03:29,460 --> 00:03:30,900
What do you mean?

48
00:03:31,840 --> 00:03:34,240
We'd be the first in the
world to welcome the year 2000.

49
00:03:34,240 --> 00:03:36,180
If we go to the island nation of Kiribati,

50
00:03:36,180 --> 00:03:39,240
we can greet tomorrow before Japan does.

51
00:03:39,900 --> 00:03:42,900
Kiribati is at the easternmost point of the International Date Line,
after all.

52
00:03:42,900 --> 00:03:45,400
That's where today ends first.

53
00:03:47,380 --> 00:03:48,620
Don't enjoy other people's misfortune!

54
00:03:49,100 --> 00:03:51,460
Well then,
this time with blood type fortune-telling

55
00:03:51,460 --> 00:03:52,420
Nah, I don't need it!

56
00:03:52,500 --> 00:03:54,000
Don't hold back, go ahead!

57
00:03:54,740 --> 00:03:56,280
Ryo-chan, what's your blood type?

58
00:03:57,300 --> 00:03:57,700
B

59
00:03:58,240 --> 00:03:58,780
B, right?

60
00:03:59,780 --> 00:04:02,400
Today's Fortune: Blood Type Championship

61
00:04:06,440 --> 00:04:10,420
Today for type B, biorhythms are
out of whack and turbulence is ahead

62
00:04:11,280 --> 00:04:13,200
Go! Yes, go! Type B!

63
00:04:15,040 --> 00:04:17,680
Your health breaks down
and you fail badly at work

64
00:04:17,680 --> 00:04:18,920
Just be careful of

65
00:04:23,300 --> 00:04:24,460
It's accurate, you know.

66
00:04:24,460 --> 00:04:27,300
It says type B should watch out for goals.

67
00:04:27,300 --> 00:04:29,020
Today's Billy is type B.

68
00:04:29,020 --> 00:04:31,140
Everything you do will fail.

69
00:04:31,140 --> 00:04:33,360
It's best to stay quietly at home.

70
00:04:36,300 --> 00:04:37,560
Look, Ryo-chan.

71
00:04:37,560 --> 00:04:39,560
This worst face-reading fortune...

72
00:04:39,560 --> 00:04:41,300
It's just like you, Ryo-chan.

73
00:04:43,920 --> 00:04:45,913
I don't know who decided this,

74
00:04:45,963 --> 00:04:48,960
but there's no way my life is going to
be controlled by something like that!

75
00:04:49,740 --> 00:04:51,460
You'd better be careful, though.

76
00:04:51,620 --> 00:04:53,557
Even the physiognomy reading
shows a face of misfortune,

77
00:04:53,607 --> 00:04:57,040
the worst crisis of your life,
watch out for tanks on Monday?

78
00:04:57,400 --> 00:05:03,480
Don't be stupid! Why would it be tanks at night?
That's unrealistic!

79
00:05:09,320 --> 00:05:11,140
It's a real tank, you know.

80
00:05:12,880 --> 00:05:14,100
It came true again.

81
00:05:18,300 --> 00:05:19,360
You idiot!

82
00:05:19,360 --> 00:05:21,040
I nearly died there!

83
00:05:21,040 --> 00:05:21,660
Sorry.

84
00:05:21,660 --> 00:05:22,940
I got chafed.

85
00:05:23,520 --> 00:05:24,520
Hand over that magazine.

86
00:05:25,120 --> 00:05:26,700
Creepy how accurate it is, damn it.

87
00:05:26,700 --> 00:05:27,900
I feel sick.

88
00:05:27,900 --> 00:05:29,020
I'll go have a word with them.

89
00:05:32,600 --> 00:05:34,680
There, it's decided!

90
00:05:35,880 --> 00:05:38,220
Aquarius: beware of water,

91
00:05:38,220 --> 00:05:43,440
as they say, fortune-telling is hit or miss.

92
00:05:43,440 --> 00:05:45,540
Sometimes it doesn't come true, after all.

93
00:05:48,920 --> 00:05:51,080
Virgo's love fortune: great misfortune.

94
00:05:51,520 --> 00:05:53,420
Break up with him right now.

95
00:05:53,420 --> 00:05:56,060
Virgo: great misfortune,
break up with your boyfriend.

96
00:05:56,060 --> 00:05:58,880
Please calm down, sir.

97
00:05:58,880 --> 00:06:01,280
Punch you?
Don't be ridiculous, that's total baloney.

98
00:06:01,280 --> 00:06:03,280
Just as I thought, Virgo's love...

99
00:06:03,280 --> 00:06:04,780
Just make it a great fortune.

100
00:06:04,780 --> 00:06:06,080
Great fortune.

101
00:06:08,020 --> 00:06:09,040
Who's responsible?

102
00:06:09,040 --> 00:06:09,900
Which one of you is it?

103
00:06:12,460 --> 00:06:13,440
H-hey, what's

104
00:06:13,440 --> 00:06:15,500
this guy's got a complaint.

105
00:06:16,120 --> 00:06:17,640
Fortune-telling's right sometimes,

106
00:06:17,640 --> 00:06:19,000
and wrong sometimes.

107
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:20,200
It can miss, too.

108
00:06:20,200 --> 00:06:22,240
No, it's the opposite. It's too accurate!

109
00:06:22,240 --> 00:06:25,860
Why is it only me who keeps getting bad luck,
just like the fortune said?

110
00:06:25,860 --> 00:06:27,980
Maybe I should do something about it.

111
00:06:27,980 --> 00:06:29,020
Editor-in-chief

112
00:06:29,020 --> 00:06:31,740
So you're the editor-in-chief?

113
00:06:36,420 --> 00:06:38,640
Allow me to hear what you have to say.

114
00:06:38,640 --> 00:06:40,360
Please, this way.

115
00:06:41,440 --> 00:06:43,600
May I take a quick look at your hand?

116
00:06:43,600 --> 00:06:47,460
I'm well versed in all kinds of fortune-telling,
so

117
00:06:48,340 --> 00:06:48,780
Well, this is

118
00:06:49,580 --> 00:06:51,840
What? Is there something wrong with my palm?

119
00:06:52,920 --> 00:06:55,600
I've never seen a life line this thick,

120
00:06:55,600 --> 00:06:59,380
but there are also many
obstruction lines cutting across it.

121
00:07:00,160 --> 00:07:02,000
Fortune-telling by hairstyle, what an idea.

122
00:07:02,640 --> 00:07:04,400
Eyebrow fortune-telling, a subtle look.

123
00:07:04,400 --> 00:07:06,780
Teeth-alignment fortune-telling,
a way of thinking.

124
00:07:06,780 --> 00:07:11,080
Whichever way you look at it,
today your luck is the worst of the worst.

125
00:07:11,080 --> 00:07:14,140
Any kind of tragedy could happen.

126
00:07:14,140 --> 00:07:14,760
What?

127
00:07:15,840 --> 00:07:18,440
What do I do? What am I supposed to do?

128
00:07:18,700 --> 00:07:19,640
What do I do?

129
00:07:20,980 --> 00:07:24,040
Getting worked up right away like
that is the worst thing you can do.

130
00:07:24,040 --> 00:07:25,980
Anger invites misfortune.

131
00:07:25,980 --> 00:07:28,720
No matter what happens,
you must never get angry.

132
00:07:29,200 --> 00:07:31,260
Fortune comes to those who laugh.

133
00:07:31,260 --> 00:07:32,300
Smile.

134
00:07:32,300 --> 00:07:33,940
A smile is the best.

135
00:07:33,940 --> 00:07:37,240
So if you keep smiling,
the misfortune stops, right?

136
00:07:39,900 --> 00:07:41,840
Just endure today.

137
00:07:41,840 --> 00:07:42,760
Hang in there.

138
00:07:50,360 --> 00:07:51,743
Our fortune guide,

139
00:07:51,793 --> 00:07:54,500
some of them really came true,
Editor-in-chief.

140
00:07:54,500 --> 00:07:56,440
Let's close up early today.

141
00:07:59,100 --> 00:08:00,900
Closing up, closing up.

142
00:08:02,080 --> 00:08:03,980
Whoa, what's this guy's problem?

143
00:08:09,400 --> 00:08:10,660
That's so bad!

144
00:08:10,660 --> 00:08:12,480
You're not supposed to make eye contact.

145
00:08:28,460 --> 00:08:57,560
Eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee...
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah

146
00:08:57,600 --> 00:09:17,400
Waaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

147
00:09:17,400 --> 00:09:19,820
I wanna quit this smile crap!
I quit, I quit, I quit!

148
00:09:19,860 --> 00:09:22,260
This misfortune isn't stopping at all,
damn it!

149
00:09:22,580 --> 00:09:23,020
Ugh, seriously!

150
00:09:28,260 --> 00:09:29,480
Give me a yakuyoke charm.

151
00:09:29,480 --> 00:09:34,800
While you're at it, give me charms for household safety,
traffic safety, passing exams, and safe childbirth.

152
00:09:35,220 --> 00:09:35,580
Here you go.

153
00:09:37,080 --> 00:09:38,060
An omikuji

154
00:09:38,480 --> 00:09:40,780
Rather than some foreign
fortune-telling I don't understand,

155
00:09:40,780 --> 00:09:43,760
omikuji advice is far more trustworthy.

156
00:09:48,560 --> 00:09:49,380
It's number nine.

157
00:09:50,220 --> 00:09:50,820
Here you go.

158
00:09:53,700 --> 00:09:56,200
Eek!

159
00:09:58,200 --> 00:09:59,880
Your wish won't come true.

160
00:10:00,020 --> 00:10:02,280
Your illness will drag on.

161
00:10:02,440 --> 00:10:04,560
Townsfolk won't come by.

162
00:10:04,820 --> 00:10:06,120
Dammit!

163
00:10:07,080 --> 00:10:08,020
One more time!

164
00:10:08,340 --> 00:10:08,660
Yes!

165
00:10:09,120 --> 00:10:09,920
Number four!

166
00:10:10,020 --> 00:10:10,940
Bad luck!

167
00:10:13,840 --> 00:10:14,860
One more time!

168
00:10:15,460 --> 00:10:15,820
Here goes!

169
00:10:16,320 --> 00:10:17,240
Number 13!

170
00:10:17,340 --> 00:10:18,600
Bad luck!

171
00:10:23,380 --> 00:10:25,737
Bad luck, more bad luck,

172
00:10:25,787 --> 00:10:27,663
and more bad luck again,

173
00:10:27,713 --> 00:10:29,880
no matter how many times I try,
it's bad luck.

174
00:10:31,280 --> 00:10:32,480
No way, that's absurd!

175
00:10:37,760 --> 00:10:39,120
Welcome back.

176
00:10:39,120 --> 00:10:42,340
Listen, nobody gets near the back room!

177
00:10:48,620 --> 00:10:50,218
Well, well,

178
00:10:50,268 --> 00:10:52,740
you really smashed it up good.

179
00:10:52,740 --> 00:10:56,340
Chief, well,
there was a little accident this morning.

180
00:10:56,340 --> 00:10:56,940
Yes.

181
00:10:58,580 --> 00:11:02,400
Never mind. All things with
form are bound to perish someday.

182
00:11:02,400 --> 00:11:03,254
Um,

183
00:11:03,304 --> 00:11:06,560
did something good happen, Chief?

184
00:11:06,560 --> 00:11:07,740
Can you tell?

185
00:11:07,740 --> 00:11:10,340
Yes, happiness is just oozing out of you.

186
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:18,760
Actually, I've been wanting a tea bowl linked to Sen no Rikyu for ages,
and an acquaintance has agreed to give it to me.

187
00:11:18,760 --> 00:11:22,940
And right after that,
I won one million yen in the lottery.

188
00:11:22,940 --> 00:11:27,460
Then I won a family trip to Okinawa
in the shopping district raffle.

189
00:11:27,460 --> 00:11:29,500
And on top of that, my grandson Daisuke...

190
00:11:29,980 --> 00:11:31,040
Wah-kah!

191
00:11:31,040 --> 00:11:34,720
Is this what they mean by
the springtime of my life?

192
00:11:34,720 --> 00:11:35,340
Here you go.

193
00:11:35,340 --> 00:11:38,220
Did you say something?

194
00:11:38,220 --> 00:11:39,060
No, sir.

195
00:11:40,340 --> 00:11:42,900
When good things keep happening,
it actually makes me anxious.

196
00:11:42,900 --> 00:11:46,740
Won't all the bad things come crashing down at once as a reaction,
sooner or later?

197
00:11:46,740 --> 00:11:48,600
It's downright terrifying, Chief.

198
00:11:48,600 --> 00:11:49,640
That's right.

199
00:11:49,640 --> 00:11:52,920
When your luck's good,
you should enjoy it to the fullest.

200
00:11:52,920 --> 00:11:54,060
Well, there's something to that.

201
00:11:54,060 --> 00:11:56,100
By the way, Ryotsu,
do you get a lot of them?

202
00:11:56,320 --> 00:12:00,640
Abdora mandora hagehoge sutaga

203
00:12:00,640 --> 00:12:03,960
Biyon boyon no tonbarage

204
00:12:03,960 --> 00:12:09,460
Abdora buddora dobitaguchon jororin no pappa

205
00:12:10,340 --> 00:12:13,460
Daan! Tadaan! No, jijirogee!

206
00:12:14,420 --> 00:12:17,468
Nandara kandara dobihabu hamuramu,

207
00:12:17,518 --> 00:12:20,069
Babyoon! Punyoon! No,

208
00:12:20,119 --> 00:12:23,379
Bakeratta taratara dobihabu babuhabu,

209
00:12:23,429 --> 00:12:24,900
Ponjarage!

210
00:12:37,180 --> 00:12:40,980
Abdora butchada paka koke kuttare!

211
00:12:40,980 --> 00:12:44,100
I'm Hyō no hanjarage!

212
00:12:44,760 --> 00:12:46,320
Who's there?

213
00:12:46,680 --> 00:12:48,040
Ryotsu, are you in there?

214
00:12:48,280 --> 00:12:49,000
Chief.

215
00:12:49,420 --> 00:12:51,200
I have a favor to ask you.

216
00:12:51,200 --> 00:12:52,560
Open this door.

217
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:53,740
No way.

218
00:12:55,060 --> 00:12:58,160
I've decided I won't leave
this room all day today.

219
00:12:58,920 --> 00:12:59,980
What about your duties?

220
00:12:59,980 --> 00:13:01,880
Open this door right now, Ryotsu.

221
00:13:01,880 --> 00:13:05,320
Even if it's the Chief's orders,
I won't open this door.

222
00:13:11,300 --> 00:13:12,440
What on earth is all this?

223
00:13:13,220 --> 00:13:14,620
They're protective charms.

224
00:13:14,620 --> 00:13:15,580
Protective charms.

225
00:13:16,560 --> 00:13:20,800
This is a full set of misfortune-warding goods
listed in the Great Encyclopedia of Protective Charms.

226
00:13:20,800 --> 00:13:22,200
Misfortune-warding.

227
00:13:22,200 --> 00:13:23,400
Unlike the Chief,

228
00:13:24,900 --> 00:13:25,500
I've been on a losing streak.

229
00:13:25,500 --> 00:13:27,800
That's left me completely disheartened.

230
00:13:29,460 --> 00:13:32,580
So you're turning to the
gods in your time of need

231
00:13:32,580 --> 00:13:33,080
Heh heh.

232
00:13:33,660 --> 00:13:35,640
Don't laugh at other people's misfortune.

233
00:13:35,640 --> 00:13:38,860
I almost forgot something important.

234
00:13:38,860 --> 00:13:41,540
Ryotsu, I need you to come
with me to the station now.

235
00:13:42,460 --> 00:13:46,280
Actually, Chief Ohara's daughter,
Oiko-san, is getting married soon.

236
00:13:46,280 --> 00:13:50,440
and we'd really like Ryotsu to be
the banquet director at the reception.

237
00:13:50,440 --> 00:13:52,720
It's a personal request
from the Chief himself.

238
00:13:52,720 --> 00:13:54,900
If anyone can liven up the celebration,

239
00:13:54,900 --> 00:13:57,500
no one can match you, senior.

240
00:13:57,900 --> 00:13:59,060
So, what do you say, Ryotsu?

241
00:13:59,060 --> 00:14:03,240
Sorry, but I'm not in the mood to
celebrate other people's happiness right now.

242
00:14:03,240 --> 00:14:07,040
Besides,
I've decided not to leave this room all day.

243
00:14:07,040 --> 00:14:09,140
Come on now.

244
00:14:09,140 --> 00:14:11,400
The station chief especially
wants you to do it.

245
00:14:11,400 --> 00:14:14,140
This is your chance to make
up for all your usual slacking.

246
00:14:14,140 --> 00:14:16,000
I hate it, I really hate it.

247
00:14:16,360 --> 00:14:20,100
You know, Chief Ohara's been on a
really lucky streak lately, Ryo-chan.

248
00:14:20,720 --> 00:14:22,860
If you stay close to a
man as lucky as the Chief,

249
00:14:22,860 --> 00:14:25,240
maybe your luck will turn around too,
Ryo-chan.

250
00:14:25,700 --> 00:14:26,060
What?

251
00:14:27,140 --> 00:14:29,620
Well, "lucky" isn't quite the word for it.

252
00:14:30,660 --> 00:14:33,560
It's more like he's hogging
all the happiness for himself.

253
00:14:40,200 --> 00:14:41,340
Are you alright, Chief?

254
00:14:42,880 --> 00:14:45,720
That stuffed toy really saved us.

255
00:14:46,900 --> 00:14:48,660
Seriously, you're so lucky.

256
00:14:53,600 --> 00:14:54,920
With a 500-yen coin.

257
00:14:54,920 --> 00:14:58,780
To think it was right at your
feet and you didn't even notice!

258
00:14:58,780 --> 00:14:59,920
Sorry.

259
00:14:59,920 --> 00:15:00,800
Yes?

260
00:15:00,800 --> 00:15:02,760
I'd like to ask for directions...

261
00:15:03,360 --> 00:15:04,760
It's here, actually.

262
00:15:05,660 --> 00:15:07,900
I seem to have gotten lost...

263
00:15:07,900 --> 00:15:08,640
Yes.

264
00:15:08,640 --> 00:15:11,000
Got it? Sorry.

265
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:13,120
No, it's my duty.

266
00:15:13,940 --> 00:15:15,140
Here, for example,

267
00:15:15,140 --> 00:15:16,500
it's simple, right?

268
00:15:18,860 --> 00:15:20,820
The Chief really is lucky.

269
00:15:20,820 --> 00:15:25,100
Even this fortune guide says the
Chief's luck is at its peak right now.

270
00:15:25,620 --> 00:15:28,020
Today is the best day in a hundred years.

271
00:15:28,020 --> 00:15:31,720
Money luck: excellent. Career luck:
excellent. Love luck: excellent.

272
00:15:31,720 --> 00:15:34,100
You'll be blessed with a wonderful day.

273
00:15:34,640 --> 00:15:38,680
Even in Ninsha astrology,
the top star is Ninsha, just like the Chief!

274
00:15:40,320 --> 00:15:41,780
Thank you very much.

275
00:15:44,560 --> 00:15:46,280
I'll come with you, Chief.

276
00:15:50,880 --> 00:15:54,240
Whether something is good or bad luck is all in how you look at it,
Ryo-san.

277
00:15:54,240 --> 00:15:57,760
Some people fail to notice that
good luck has come their way,

278
00:15:57,760 --> 00:16:02,500
while plenty of others live cheerfully and
resiliently even in the midst of misfortune.

279
00:16:02,500 --> 00:16:05,000
Standing next to the
Chief makes me feel safe.

280
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:07,860
My shoelace...

281
00:16:09,020 --> 00:16:09,960
Chief?

282
00:16:11,400 --> 00:16:12,120
Whoa!

283
00:16:13,820 --> 00:16:14,620
W-what is it?

284
00:16:15,720 --> 00:16:18,800
Sorry about that, my hand slipped.

285
00:16:18,800 --> 00:16:20,540
I wonder if it's gone now.

286
00:16:22,140 --> 00:16:24,620
The moment I'm apart from the Chief,
this happens.

287
00:16:24,620 --> 00:16:27,640
I'm never leaving the Chief's side again.

288
00:16:28,200 --> 00:16:29,000
What's that?

289
00:16:29,420 --> 00:16:31,740
Those two were walking like this before too.

290
00:16:31,740 --> 00:16:32,560
Don't look.

291
00:16:33,020 --> 00:16:34,900
Ew, it's a pair of police officers,
a couple.

292
00:16:35,320 --> 00:16:36,560
That's embarrassing.

293
00:16:36,560 --> 00:16:38,320
They're coming out, aren't they?

294
00:16:38,320 --> 00:16:39,460
Let's cheer them on!

295
00:16:40,180 --> 00:16:42,920
People will get the wrong idea,
so could you move a bit apart!

296
00:16:43,080 --> 00:16:45,440
No way! I'm never letting go!

297
00:16:46,120 --> 00:16:47,640
I said, let go!

298
00:16:47,720 --> 00:16:48,620
No way!

299
00:16:48,800 --> 00:16:49,800
Let go!

300
00:16:50,060 --> 00:16:50,740
I said no!

301
00:16:50,980 --> 00:16:52,020
Get off!

302
00:16:52,120 --> 00:16:52,620
I don't want to!

303
00:16:53,240 --> 00:16:54,640
Let go of me!

304
00:16:54,740 --> 00:16:55,120
No!

305
00:16:55,140 --> 00:16:57,440
I said let go! Enough of this nonsense!

306
00:16:57,600 --> 00:16:57,840
Found it, found it!

307
00:17:18,520 --> 00:17:19,680
Are you all right, Ryotsu?

308
00:17:19,680 --> 00:17:22,340
Thud!

309
00:17:33,380 --> 00:17:35,800
Please don't leave me behind!

310
00:17:38,800 --> 00:17:39,620
Pchuun!

311
00:17:43,120 --> 00:17:44,400
So you were waiting, Pchuun!

312
00:17:44,580 --> 00:17:45,540
I'll catch you!

313
00:17:45,560 --> 00:17:46,080
Let's go!

314
00:17:46,240 --> 00:17:46,900
Don't let go of me!

315
00:17:59,700 --> 00:18:01,220
I told you to get off!

316
00:18:01,340 --> 00:18:01,980
I refuse!

317
00:18:54,340 --> 00:18:56,580
It's your duty, your duty, you bastard!

318
00:19:00,280 --> 00:19:01,060
Come on, Chief!

319
00:19:01,520 --> 00:19:03,440
Please don't leave me behind!

320
00:19:04,840 --> 00:19:05,620
H-hey!

321
00:19:05,640 --> 00:19:06,760
Hey, hey, hey!

322
00:19:07,020 --> 00:19:08,440
Don't grab me there, hey!

323
00:19:08,440 --> 00:19:08,960
I don't get it!

324
00:19:09,520 --> 00:19:37,940
Nooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooo!

325
00:19:39,520 --> 00:19:40,340
My apologies.

326
00:20:04,060 --> 00:20:05,440
Speaking of you...

327
00:20:05,440 --> 00:20:08,000
It seems even my good luck is running away.

328
00:20:10,740 --> 00:20:13,480
Because today's fortune
is the worst possible.

329
00:20:14,900 --> 00:20:19,200
If you go to Kiribati,
you'll greet tomorrow a step ahead of Japan!

330
00:20:19,760 --> 00:20:21,160
That's right, Kiribati!

331
00:20:27,860 --> 00:20:30,100
Kiribati! Go to Kiribati!

332
00:20:30,100 --> 00:20:31,200
Kiribati.

333
00:20:39,040 --> 00:20:41,040
Just what is this Kiribati, anyway?

334
00:20:41,040 --> 00:20:41,880
Right here, right here.

335
00:20:43,240 --> 00:20:44,460
Is it really that far?

336
00:20:45,000 --> 00:20:47,040
We're really running low on fuel!

337
00:20:49,820 --> 00:20:50,620
There it is.

338
00:20:52,520 --> 00:20:53,420
Alright, go!

339
00:21:00,140 --> 00:21:01,120
What's with that guy?

340
00:21:01,860 --> 00:21:03,120
Hitchhiking!

341
00:21:03,120 --> 00:21:03,840
Run!

342
00:21:07,880 --> 00:21:08,560
Wait!

343
00:21:16,400 --> 00:21:17,900
We're going, Chief!

344
00:21:17,900 --> 00:21:19,860
Why do I have to go through this?

345
00:21:19,860 --> 00:21:20,400
One, two, go!

346
00:21:20,400 --> 00:21:21,640
Here we go.

347
00:21:26,480 --> 00:21:27,120
Whoa!

348
00:21:27,200 --> 00:21:27,820
You idiot!

349
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:43,080
A jet next? Right, this time it's that one!

350
00:21:43,480 --> 00:21:44,780
Full throttle!

351
00:21:49,920 --> 00:21:51,860
Alright, here we go! Ready... go!

352
00:21:53,420 --> 00:21:54,260
Kiribati!

353
00:21:57,260 --> 00:21:59,000
Apparently the air currents are rough.

354
00:22:05,120 --> 00:22:05,920
Whoa, whoa!

355
00:22:07,780 --> 00:22:09,740
Surely not up that high...

356
00:22:09,740 --> 00:22:12,180
Waiting around in this
crowded mess won't cut it.

357
00:22:16,460 --> 00:22:17,400
It's a jumbo jet!

358
00:22:25,440 --> 00:22:28,200
Here we go, Chief.

359
00:22:28,200 --> 00:22:29,800
Ready... go!

360
00:22:32,460 --> 00:22:34,840
Kiribati.

361
00:22:45,940 --> 00:22:48,760
Kiribati

362
00:23:02,760 --> 00:23:04,860
Yes! We finally made it!

363
00:23:04,860 --> 00:23:06,400
So this is Kiribati!

364
00:23:07,600 --> 00:23:08,680
Aloha!

365
00:23:08,680 --> 00:23:12,980
Welcome to Hawaii!

366
00:23:12,980 --> 00:23:15,780
Hawaii? That means...

367
00:23:28,560 --> 00:23:31,900
We must have crossed the
International Date Line.

368
00:23:31,900 --> 00:23:34,300
It's still Monday in Hawaii.

369
00:23:37,120 --> 00:23:40,440
You're still the same
slippery fool from yesterday.

370
00:23:40,440 --> 00:23:43,860
Your worst day of your life
has started all over again.

371
00:23:52,380 --> 00:23:55,020
Bad luck is starting again.

372
00:24:14,300 --> 00:24:19,580
Every train ride home, a nap on my back.

373
00:24:20,620 --> 00:24:25,780
Another tough week, the hard work and the strain,
all quite understandable.

374
00:24:27,140 --> 00:24:30,640
Bucket in hand, playing it cool.

375
00:24:30,640 --> 00:24:33,440
Beef bowl, extra sauce, cloudy with sauce.

376
00:24:33,440 --> 00:24:36,700
The irritation from endless overtime too,

377
00:24:36,700 --> 00:24:40,340
irritation melts away, and I feel refreshed.

378
00:24:43,860 --> 00:24:50,120
Every day's no problem,
once I step through a hot shower.

379
00:24:50,120 --> 00:24:56,680
Every day's no problem,
a restful pillow restores my energy.

380
00:24:59,640 --> 00:25:06,300
Every day's no problem,
I really love a girl like me.

381
00:25:06,300 --> 00:25:13,020
Every day's no problem,
Monday when the carts are flying.

382
00:25:21,100 --> 00:25:23,400
Sandy, glad you came!

383
00:25:23,400 --> 00:25:25,840
Could it be you couldn't forget about me,

384
00:25:25,840 --> 00:25:27,940
that you came all the way from America?

385
00:25:28,340 --> 00:25:30,440
Is that really so?

386
00:25:30,780 --> 00:25:33,540
On top of that, Dad and Mom
are both keen on the wedding too.

387
00:25:34,160 --> 00:25:37,360
Next time, love across the sea,
see you then.

388
00:25:38,320 --> 00:25:40,700
Over there, there's Kame-ari.

389
00:25:41,720 --> 00:25:44,040
Surely there's Kame-ari.

390
00:25:45,320 --> 00:25:49,140
Everyone, come on over to our town!

